# The MOOD macro: the ALGORITHM dial is the mood (0.17.16: on every page but Chords and Global; Perform before), 0 (chill) .. 100 (peak), 50 as the piece is. The engine is given
# each listed setting moved by its share (here the acid's density, 60 in the first piece, by 30 at the ends); the piece keeps its own.
seed 0
wait 3000
expect mood 50
expect moodacid 60
tap HOME
wait 100
expect view 37
turn ALGO 5
wait 100
expect mood 60
expect moodacid 66
turn ALGO 20
wait 100
expect mood 100
expect moodacid 90
shot mood_peak.png
turn ALGO -50
wait 100
expect mood 0
expect moodacid 30
shot mood_chill.png
# (0.17.16) off the perform screen the dial is the mood too (the Tempo page)
tap HOME
wait 100
expect view 0
turn ALGO 1
wait 100
expect mood 2
# on Global it is the mode, the mood stays
tap GLO
wait 100
expect view 32
turn ALGO 1
wait 100
expect mood 2
expect par72 6
turn ALGO -1
wait 100
expect par72 5
# back to the middle on Perform: the piece as it is
tap HOME
wait 100
tap HOME
wait 400
tap HOME
wait 100
expect view 37
turn ALGO 24
wait 100
expect mood 50
expect moodacid 60
